-- Constructors (operator, 2026-11-12): `<entity> = Class(name: value, ...)`. The TARGET on the left is the entity's identity (no `key` argument, no declared identity). It creates the entity at that eid
-- by the creation path of a write (the class must be one the pack owns or imports; refused otherwise, as a receipt, never a crash), sets the named arguments as its first properties, and is idempotent:
-- an entity that exists is not created again and a property that already has a value is not overwritten. A target whose eid prefix is not the class (`membrane::Config:...` built as `Voice(...)`) is
-- stamped `parents: ['cls:voice']`, the ISA kind-mirror, so the engine mirrors it by kind. Converted from tests/constructors_1143.rs; what stays Rust there is what looks at the engine's own
-- birth events and refusals lists, the print/parse round trip and the static type.
-- Each test writes `Box:a.go` twice: the second write of the same value changes nothing, a second `go` is a fresh trigger.

test a constructor creates the target with its arguments as properties
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:t1 = Thing(kind: 'in', n: this.n + 1)
given Box:a {"n": 4}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
eval Thing:t1.cls = "Thing"
reads Thing:t1.kind = "in"
reads Thing:t1.n = 5
-- the prefix is the class: no kind stamp
reads Thing:t1.parents = null

test the target is the identity a key in brackets names it
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:slot[this.slug] = Thing(kind: 'x')
    Reply:r[this.n]:part = Reply(text: 'hi')
given Box:a {"slug": "ann-b", "n": 3}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
reads Thing:slot:ann-b.kind = "x"
reads Reply:r:3:part.text = "hi"

test a foreign prefix is stamped with the kind so the engine mirrors it
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    membrane::Config:voice:in[this.slug] = Thing(kind: 'in')
    membrane::Chat:message[this.n]:response = Reply(text: 'hi')
given Box:a {"slug": "ann-b", "n": 9}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
reads membrane::Config:voice:in:ann-b.kind = "in"
-- the eid class first (the birth default), then the stamp
reads membrane::Config:voice:in:ann-b.parents = ["cls:config", "cls:thing"]
-- it stays the class its eid names (the Python seat's)
eval ${'membrane::Config:voice:in:ann-b'}['cls'] = "Config"
reads membrane::Chat:message:9:response.parents = ["cls:chat", "cls:reply"]
reads membrane::Chat:message:9:response.text = "hi"

test a constructor is idempotent and never overwrites a value
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:t1 = Thing(kind: 'new', n: 1, note: None)
given Box:a {}
given Thing:t1 {"kind": "old", "n": null}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
-- a property that has a value stays
reads Thing:t1.kind = "old"
-- an unset one is filled
reads Thing:t1.n = 1
-- a null argument sets nothing
reads Thing:t1.note = null

test a foreign entity that exists keeps what it has and gains only what is unset
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    membrane::Config:voice:in:z = Thing(kind: 'in', person: 'Z')
given Box:a {}
given membrane::Config:voice:in:z {"person": "Zed", "parents": ["cls:thing"]}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
reads membrane::Config:voice:in:z.person = "Zed"
reads membrane::Config:voice:in:z.kind = "in"
-- the birth default put the eid class first; the constructor added nothing to the list the entity was given
reads membrane::Config:voice:in:z.parents = ["cls:config", "cls:thing"]

test a class the pack does not own or import is refused with a reason
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:t1 = Nope(kind: 'in')
    Thing:t2 = Goal(kind: 'in')
    Thing:t3 = Thing(kind: 'ok')
given Box:a {}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
-- no pack owns Nope
absent Thing:t1
-- goalgraph owns Goal and this pack does not import it
absent Thing:t2
-- the line below still runs
reads Thing:t3.kind = "ok"

test a null or bad key creates nothing
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Reply.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:k[this.missing] = Thing(kind: 'x')
    Thing:k[this.f] = Thing(kind: 'x')
given Box:a {"f": 1.5}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
eval len(instances('Thing')) = 0

test a constructor with positional arguments is refused when the pack loads
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:x = Thing(1, 2)
error: named

test a constructor with a positional argument after a named one is refused
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:x = Thing(a: 1, 2)
error: named

test a constructor with a repeated name is refused
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Thing:x = Thing(a: 1, a: 2)
error: twice

test a constructor outside a write target is a reasoned error not a crash
PACK t 1
Thing.shown getter: this.eid
Box.g getter: Thing(kind: 'x')
given Box:a {}
reads Box:a.g = null
eval 'constructor' in why(Box:a.g) = true

test a foreign prefix entity gets its kinds getters at once
-- the kind stamp (`parents`) is set after the birth: the kind's getters must still be computed for what was just made
PACK t 1
Voice.shown getter: 'v:' + this.eid
Voice.twice getter: this.n * 2
Box.go on-setter t:
  ALWAYS:
    Config:x = Voice(n: 4)
given Box:a {}
write Box:a.go = 1
write Box:a.go = 2
reads Config:x.parents = ["cls:config", "cls:voice"]
reads Config:x.shown = "v:Config:x"
reads Config:x.twice = 8
